# Engineering discipline

Full workflow: `skills/engineering-discipline/SKILL.md`. Apply on plan reviews, critiques, and feature work.

## 1. Review closeout

Every critique item gets one disposition before the session ends: **Accepted**, **Rejected**, **Deferred**, or **Needs option**. End with a decision ledger table — not findings alone.

## 2. Test depth

Turn every planned check from reviews into a named test (`src/lib/*.test.ts` or E2E). Prefer unit tests for access, env/mode guards, and token/booking logic. Run `npm test` after adding tests.

## 3. Simplification

Every feature plan names what gets **removed**, **split**, or **merged** — not only risks. Flag files approaching 500 lines and legacy paths (mock data, `NODE_ENV` branches, dev-only routes) this work replaces.

## Session end

Close with: decision counts, test files touched, simplification actions (or justified none), and one next action.
